flowchart TD
    PT[Proof Techniques] --> D[Direct Proof]
    PT --> CON[Contrapositive]
    PT --> CTR[Contradiction]
    PT --> IN[Mathematical Induction]
    PT --> SI[Strong Induction]
    PT --> CE[Counterexample]
    PT --> EX[Existence Proofs]
    PT --> PC[Proof by Cases]

    D --> D1["Assume P is true"]
    D --> D2["Derive Q using logic"]
    D --> D3[Example: even n implies even n-squared]

    CON --> C1["Prove NOT Q implies NOT P"]
    CON --> C2[Equivalent to original statement]
    CON --> C3[Example: odd n-squared implies odd n]

    CTR --> CR1["Assume statement is false"]
    CTR --> CR2["Derive contradiction"]
    CTR --> CR3[Example: sqrt 2 is irrational]

    IN --> I1[Base case Pn0]
    IN --> I2["Inductive step Pk implies Pk+1"]
    IN --> I3[Example: sum 1 to n = nn+1/2]

    SI --> S1[Multiple base cases]
    SI --> S2["Assume all smaller cases Pn0 ... Pk"]
    SI --> S3[Example: prime factorization]

    CE --> E1[Find one counterexample]
    CE --> E2[Disproves universal claim]

    EX --> X1[Constructive provide example]
    EX --> X2[Non-constructive prove existence]

    PC --> P1[Divide domain into cases]
    PC --> P2[Prove each case separately]
